  "id": "COMPOUND:19397 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship between (E)-N-Isobutylundeca-2-En-8,10-Diynamide and SN12K1, with the compound acting as a target for several enzymes. The first step involves the compound directly targeting CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, an enzyme involved in sialylation processes. This enzyme is then identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one. These latter compounds are themselves targets of SN12K1, indicating a chain of interactions where (E)-N-Isobutylundeca-2-En-8,10-Diynamide indirectly influences SN12K1 through its effects on the sialyltransferase enzyme. The evidence suggests that the compound may modulate SN12K1 via a pathway involving sialyltransferase activity, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
